.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_MERGE_NODE 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_merge_node ,
.Nm ndi_merge_wildcard_node
.Nd merge driver configuration properties into hardware nodes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_merge_node
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "int (*make_ua)(dev_info_t *, char *, int)"
.Fc
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_merge_wildcard_node
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va dip
Nonpersistent source node created from a driver configuration file.
.It Va make_ua
Callback that writes a null-terminated unit address and returns
\fBDDI_SUCCESS\fP, or returns \fBDDI_FAILURE\fP to skip a child.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Nexus drivers use these functions during child initialization to apply
\fBdriver.conf\fP properties to enumerated hardware nodes.
The caller must own the parent's critical section and \fBdip\fP must be a
nonpersistent configuration-file node.
.Pp
\fBndi_merge_node()\fP requires a unit address on \fBdip\fP.
It searches siblings by driver binding and address, using \fBmake_ua\fP to obtain
addresses for unnamed children as described in
\fBndi_devi_findchild_by_callback(9F)\fP.
If the target is persistent, has not been initialized, and has no system or
driver properties, the system and driver property lists are transferred from
\fBdip\fP to the target.
Hardware properties are not transferred.
.Pp
A matching node that is already initialized, already has properties, or is
another configuration-file node is still treated as a recognized merge target.
Success therefore does not guarantee that properties were transferred.
The nexus is responsible for rejecting or disposing of the source merge node
through its child-initialization protocol.
.Pp
\fBndi_merge_wildcard_node()\fP copies the source properties to each eligible
persistent sibling bound to the same driver.
The source must be bound to a valid driver major number.
Initialized siblings and siblings with existing system or driver properties
are skipped.
.Sh CONTEXT
These functions may be called from user or kernel context.
They may sleep.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
\fBndi_merge_node()\fP returns \fBDDI_SUCCESS\fP if it recognizes a matching
merge target, including cases where no properties are transferred.
It returns \fBDDI_FAILURE\fP when no other matching node exists.
\fBndi_merge_wildcard_node()\fP has no return value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr driver.conf 5 ,
.Xr ndi_devi_enter 9F ,
.Xr ndi_devi_findchild 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
